 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "The chef is fed up with Max's naps, but Max is fed up with peeling bananas. Barinov gives him his first real job: cooking staff lunch, with a warning about what happens if they don't like it. Here's the Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Здесь не ночлежка, а работа!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф, вы всё равно не даёте мне готовить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я уже отклеил все этикетки от бананов.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Хорошо, хочешь готовить — будешь готовить!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Внимание, повара ресторана!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Сегодня обед для персонала готовит наш огузок.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это очень ответственное задание.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Если им не понравится, они съедят тебя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты меня понял?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Да, шеф, я всё понял.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я так мечтал готовить на кухне.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ну что, ты доволен?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я очень рад, шеф, только выпью кофе.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Быстро переодевайся, работаем!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go through the chef's offer.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Здесь не ночлежка, а работа!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is not a shelter, but work!' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "ночлежка,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the Russian expression for a dosshouse, built from a word for a night's lodging. The structure used here literally translates to 'not X but Y'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Шеф, вы всё равно не даёте мне готовить.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Chef, you still won't let me cook.' The phrase ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "всё равно",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally means 'all the same', meaning still. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "не даёте мне готовить.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'you don't give me to cook', which is the phrase for 'won't let me'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я уже отклеил все этикетки от бананов.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I already peeled all labels from the bananas.' The action word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "отклеил",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is built from a starting piece meaning 'off', combined with a word meaning 'to glue', resulting in 'unglued'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "этикетки",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the term for labels, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "от бананов.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'from the bananas'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Хорошо, хочешь готовить — будешь готовить!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Fine, you want to cook — you will cook!' The halves mirror each other: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "хочешь готовить",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", you want to cook, then ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "— будешь готовить!",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning you will cook.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Внимание, повара ресторана!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Attention, cooks of the restaurant!' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Внимание,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the phrase for 'attention'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "повара",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning cooks, takes an 'a' sound for multiple people, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "ресторана!",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'of the restaurant'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Сегодня обед для персонала готовит наш огузок.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Today our Oguzok is cooking lunch for the staff.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "обед",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the expression for the midday meal. The doer of the action, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "наш огузок.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", comes last, so the new information lands at the end.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Это очень ответственное задание.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is a very important assignment.' The describing word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "ответственное",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning responsible, is built from a word meaning answer: a job you answer for. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "задание.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally means something set for you.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Если им не понравится, они съедят тебя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'If they don't like it, they will eat you.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "им не понравится,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'to them it won't be pleasing'. The phrase for 'they will eat up', ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "съедят",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", is built from a little piece meaning finishing the whole thing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты меня понял?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Did you understand me?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты меня понял?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to 'you me understood?'. The action word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "понял?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " has a special ending because a man is being addressed.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Да, шеф, я всё понял.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yes, Chef, I understood everything.' Max repeats the action word, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "всё понял.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " meaning understood everything, adding the Russian term for 'everything'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Я так мечтал готовить на кухне.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I dreamed so much of cooking in the kitchen.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "мечтал",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the action word meaning to dream, shaped for a man talking about what already happened. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "так",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the translation for 'so much', and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "на кухне.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
